r _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> What it is <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> : the final â€œSentinelâ€ score (a scalar). <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> : feature  (your measured inputs, indicators, signals). <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> : weight for feature  (how strongly that feature pushes the score). <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> : bias / intercept term. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Important nuance <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> As written, youâ€™re adding  inside the sum: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> \sum_{i=1}^n (W_iX_i + B) = \sum_{i=1}^n W_iX_i + \sum_{i=1}^n B <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> = \sum_{i=1}^n W_iX_i + nB <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> So the bias effectively becomes . <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> If you intended a single global bias (common in scoring models), the usual form is: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> \Phi_{\text{sentinel}}=\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n}W_iX_i\right) + B\ \pm\ \Delta_{11.3} <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Both are valid, they just mean different things: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Bias-per-feature:  grows as you add more features. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Global bias:  is a single offset for the whole model. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> The  term <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Thatâ€™s your uncertainty / tolerance / margin band. It reads like: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> â€œCompute the score, but treat it as reliable only within Â± 11.3 units (or whatever units  uses).â€ <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Depending on what you mean,  could be: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> a fixed measurement error bound <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> a safety margin <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> a confidence interval half-width <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> a â€œreal-world slop factorâ€ youâ€™ve empirically chosen <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> A quick numeric example <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Say , , , and . <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> If bias is inside the sum: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c1622755516="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><