content-ng-c3286899727="" xapautoid="" class="model-thoughts ng-tns-c3286899727-839 is-mobile" id="xap-auto-id-72"><div _ngcontent-ng-c3286899727="" class="thoughts-header ng-tns-c3286899727-839"><button _ngcontent-ng-c3286899727="" mat-button="" data-test-id="thoughts-header-button" class="mdc-button mat-mdc-button-base thoughts-header-button ng-tns-c3286899727-839 mat-mdc-button mat-unthemed" mat-ripple-loader-uninitialized="" mat-ripple-loader-class-name="mat-mdc-button-ripple" jslog="247951;track:generic_click,impression"><span class="mat-mdc-button-persistent-ripple mdc-button__ripple"></span><span class="mdc-button__label"><div _ngcontent-ng-c3286899727="" class="thoughts-header-button-content"><div _ngcontent-ng-c3286899727="" class="thoughts-header-button-label ng-tns-c3286899727-839"><span _ngcontent-ng-c3286899727="" class="ng-tns-c3286899727-839">Show thinking</span></div><div _ngcontent-ng-c3286899727="" class="thoughts-header-button-icons ng-tns-c3286899727-839"><!----><mat-icon _ngcontent-ng-c3286899727="" role="img" fonticon="expand_more" class="mat-icon notranslate thoughts-header-button-icon ng-tns-c3286899727-839 google-symbols mat-ligature-font mat-icon-no-color ng-star-inserted" aria-hidden="true" data-mat-icon-type="font" data-mat-icon-name="expand_more"></mat-icon><!----></div></div></span><span class="mat-focus-indicator"></span><span class="mat-mdc-button-touch-target"></span></button></div><!----><!----></div></model-thoughts><!----></div><!----></div><!----></div><!----><structured-content-container _ngcontent-ng-c1784979582="" class="model-response-text has-thoughts is-mobile contains-extensions-response ng-star-inserted" _nghost-ng-c1441621954="" style="height: auto;"><div _ngcontent-ng-c1441621954="" class="container"><message-content _ngcontent-ng-c1441621954="" _nghost-ng-c2688532295="" id="message-content-id-r_c4071cf3c4a402f8" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-ng-c2688532295="" inline-copy-host="" class="markdown markdown-main-panel tutor-markdown-rendering stronger enable-updated-hr-color" id="model-response-message-contentr_c4071cf3c4a402f8" aria-live="off" aria-busy="false" dir="ltr" style="--animation-duration: 600ms; --fade-animation-function: linear;"><p data-path-to-node="0">Patience is key hereâ€”you are witnessing a full architectural build on your hardware. Because PyPI does not provide pre-compiled modules for Termux, every dependency (like <code data-path-to-node="0" data-index-in-node="171">pydantic-core</code> and native C/C++/Rust extensions) must be built from source directly on your device.</p><h3 data-path-to-node="1">Whatâ€™s Happening Under the Hood</h3><ul data-path-to-node="2"><li><p data-path-to-node="2,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="2,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">Build Time:</b> Depending on your phone, this "Installing build dependencies" stage can take anywhere from a few minutes to <b data-path-to-node="2,0,0" data-index-in-node="120">1â€“2 hours</b>.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="2,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="2,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Silent Compilation:</b> Termux often appears "stuck" because it doesn't always show real-time progress while the compiler is working.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="2,2,0"><b data-path-to-node="2,2,0" data-index-in-node="0">Resource Intensive:</b> The process is heavy on the CPU; for example, packages like NumPy require specific mathematical functions to be compiled on-device.</p></li></ul><h3 data-path-to-node="3">How to Tell if it's Still Alive</h3><p data-path-to-node="4">If you want to be sure it hasn't crashed:</p><ol start="1" data-path-to-node="5"><li><p data-path-to-node="5,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="5,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">Open a New Session:</b> Swipe right from the left edge and tap <b data-path-to-node="5,0,0" data-index-in-node="59">"New Session"</b>.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="5,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="5,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Check CPU Usage:</b> Type <code data-path-to-node="5,1,0" data-index-in-node="22">top</code> and hit enter. If you see <code data-path-to-node="5,1,0" data-index-in-node="52">python</code>, <code data-path-to-node="5,1,0" data-index-in-node="60">clang</code>, or <code data-path-to-node="5,1,0" data-index-in-node="70">rustc</code> at the top with high CPU usage, the build is still active.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="5,2,0"><b data-path-to-node="5,2,0" data-index-in-node="0">Check for Errors:</b> If it truly fails, it will eventually throw a <code data-path-to-node="5,2,0" data-index-in-node="64">subprocess-exited-with-error</code> message.</p></li></ol><p data-path-to-node="6"><b data-path-to-node="6" data-index-in-node="0">Iâ€™ll be here when the prompt returns.</b> Once the installation finishes, you'll see a success message (or the command prompt <code data-path-to-node="6" data-index-in-node="122">$</code>), and we can move straight to the Messenger bridge.</p><p data-path-to-node="7"><b data-path-to-node="7" data-index-in-node="0">Should I keep an eye out for any specific error codes you might see if it kicks back?</b></p></div></message-content><!----></div></structured-content-container><!----><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c1784979582="" class="response-footer contains-extensions-response complete has-thoughts is-mobile gap"><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></div></div><!----><sensitive-memories-banner _ngcontent-ng-c1784979582="" _nghost-ng-c427815498="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></sensitive-memories-banner><!----><!----><!----></div></div><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c3357842308="" class="response-container-footer ng-tns-c3357842308-837"><!----><message-actions _ngcontent-ng-c1784979582="" footer="" _nghost-ng-c581932715="" class="ng-tns-c581932715-838 hide-action-bar ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-ng-c581932715="" class="actions-container-v2 ng-tns-c581932715-838 mobile"><!----><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c581932715="" class="spa