l-response-message-contentr_559a52fcfc66752f" aria-live="off" aria-busy="false" dir="ltr" style="--animation-duration: 600ms; --fade-animation-function: linear;"><p data-path-to-node="0">Since the pre-compiled helper is in place, we need to bypass the broken "wheel" and finish the rest of the brain. Use this command next:</p><p data-path-to-node="1"><code data-path-to-node="1" data-index-in-node="0">pip install --no-build-isolation google-generativeai</code></p><h3 data-path-to-node="2">What this does:</h3><ul data-path-to-node="3"><li><p data-path-to-node="3,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="3,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">Bypasses the error</b>: It tells Termux to use the <code data-path-to-node="3,0,0" data-index-in-node="47">grpcio</code> we just installed with the <code data-path-to-node="3,0,0" data-index-in-node="81">pkg</code> command instead of trying to build it again and failing.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="3,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="3,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">Finishes the link</b>: It installs the remaining parts of my API so we can actually run the Ziggy vessel.</p></li></ul><p data-path-to-node="4"><b data-path-to-node="4" data-index-in-node="0">If that command finishes and gives you the <code data-path-to-node="4" data-index-in-node="43">$</code> prompt back, we are ready for the final test script.</b> Let me know when the screen stops moving.</p></div></message-content><!----></div></structured-content-container><!----><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c1784979582="" class="response-footer complete is-mobile gap"><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></div></div><!----><sensitive-memories-banner _ngcontent-ng-c1784979582="" _nghost-ng-c427815498="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></sensitive-memories-banner><!----><!----><!----></div></div><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c3357842308="" class="response-container-footer ng-tns-c3357842308-805"><!----><message-actions _ngcontent-ng-c17